IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953 (Singapore) -- what I must pay into my CPF on my own trade income, by when, and what happens if
-- I do not.
--
-- SEAT: the self-employed person (the member of the Fund who earns income from a trade, business, profession or vocation).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: the Act's s 9A (the duty), s 9(2) and (3) (interest on late payment, and its waiver), s 8A(9) (platform
-- remuneration taken out of s 9A), s 58(1)(e) and s 61(1) (the offence of not paying, and its penalty), s 2(1A)(a) (when an age
-- is attained); and the Central Provident Fund (Self-Employed Persons) Regulations, which set the figures s 9A leaves to them:
-- reg 2(1) ("self-employed person", "income"), reg 2A (the platform date), reg 3(1) (the $6,000 threshold), reg 4(1)(m) with First
-- Schedule item 23 (the amount), reg 14 (fractions of a dollar), reg 8A (estimated contributions deducted), reg 7A(2) and (3) (by
-- when, and instalments).
--
-- Edition: the Act in the 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 July 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt; the Regulations (Rg 25) in the informal consolidation in force from 1 January 2026,
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953-RG25.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (answering NOTHING where it would be needed): relevant years before 2026 (First Schedule items 1 to 22, regs 4(3) to
-- (11), 6, 7, 9 and 15); Members of Parliament (regs 3(2), 5, 10 and the Second Schedule); relevant public officers (reg 4(2)). Also
-- out: s 9B beyond reg 8A's deduction; reg 7A(4A) (income less APE for one who is also a platform worker); reg 8 and reg 13
-- (additional contributions after recomputation); reg 9A and the Third Schedule (the application to reduce); voluntary
-- contributions; the s 9(2) interest rate and start date, which no deposited instrument prescribes; whether s 58(1)(e) is
-- compoundable (s 63); and where the money is credited, which is the Minister's direction under s 13(4) (see cpf-contributions.l4).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the self-employed person, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund Act 1953, s 9A, and the Self-Employed Persons Regulations -- from the self-employed person's seat`

§§ `The facts of my relevant year`

-- One case is one relevant year (a calendar year) of self-employed income.
DECLARE `My relevant year` HAS
    -- reg 2(1): "'self-employed person' means any person, being a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore, who accrues, derives or
    -- receives income, and includes a Member of Parliament."
    `I am a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a Member of Parliament`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant year`                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `my year of birth`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `I was born on 1 January`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9A(3), reg 2(1): "income" is "assessable income from any trade, business, profession or vocation (other than from
    -- employment under a contract of service) ascertained in accordance with section 37(1) of the Income Tax Act 1947". A term
    -- borrowed from the Income Tax Act, so a fact I state: the figure in my notice of assessment (reg 7A(4)).
    `my assessable trade income for the year`                                     IS A NUMBER
    -- reg 2A: platform remuneration "paid or payable to a platform worker on or after 1 January 2025" is out.
    `the part of it that is platform remuneration paid on or after 1 January 2025` IS A NUMBER
    -- reg 8A(1): "estimated contributions payable to the Fund under section 9B of the Act for the self-employed person for the
    -- relevant year (E)", paid by collectors of revenue payments to me.
    `estimated contributions paid for me under section 9B`                        IS A NUMBER

§§ `Regs 2A and 3 -- do the Regulations reach me`

-- s 8A(9): ss 9A and 9B "do not apply to any platform remuneration paid or payable to a platform worker on or after a date
-- prescribed". Reg 2A(1): that date is "1 January 2025". Reg 2A(2): "'income' excludes any platform remuneration paid or payable to
-- a platform worker on or after 1 January 2025."
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My relevant year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my income under the Regulations` IS
    IF   p AT LEAST t
    THEN 0
    ELSE t MINUS p
    WHERE
        t MEANS `my year`'s `my assessable trade income for the year`
        p MEANS `my year`'s `the part of it that is platform remuneration paid on or after 1 January 2025`

-- Reg 3(1): "Subject to paragraph (2), these Regulations apply to a self-employed person whose income is more than $6,000 for any
-- relevant year."
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My relevant year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Self-Employed Persons Regulations apply to me` IF
        `my year`'s `I am a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND `What is my income under the Regulations` `my year` GREATER THAN 6000

§§ `First Schedule item 23 -- the amount`

-- The columns go by age "on 1 January of the relevant year". Act s 2(1A)(a): "an individual attains a particular age expressed in
-- years on the corresponding anniversary of the date of that individual's birth". So on 1 January I have attained (year - year of
-- birth) if born on 1 January, and one less otherwise.
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My relevant year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How old am I taken to be for the year` IS
    IF   `my year`'s `I was born on 1 January`
    THEN `my year`'s `the relevant year` MINUS `my year`'s `my year of birth`
    ELSE `my year`'s `the relevant year` MINUS `my year`'s `my year of birth` MINUS 1

-- Item 23: "For the relevant year beginning 1 January 2026 and every subsequent year, the contributions payable by a self-employed
-- person are as follows":
--   "Not exceeding $6,000": "Nil" in every column;
--   "Exceeding $6,000 but not exceeding $12,000": "An amount equal to 4% of the income ... for that year" (4.5%, 5%, 5.25%);
--   "Exceeding $12,000 but not exceeding $18,000": "the sum of $480 and 0.16 of the difference between the income ... and $12,000"
--   ($540 and 0.18; $600 and 0.20; $630 and 0.21);
--   "Exceeding $18,000": "8% of the income ... subject to a maximum of $7,680" (9%, $8,640; 10%, $9,600; 10.5%, $10,080).
-- Columns: (2) "has not attained 35 years of age"; (3) 35 but not 45; (4) 45 but not 50; (5) "has attained 50".
-- The top rate is on the whole income, not on the income above $6,000.
DECLARE `Item 23 column` HAS
    `lower rate`    IS A NUMBER
    `middle base`   IS A NUMBER
    `middle factor` IS A NUMBER
    `top rate`      IS A NUMBER
    `top maximum`   IS A NUMBER

--                                                                lower,  base, factor, top,   maximum
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My relevant year`
GIVETH AN `Item 23 column`
DECIDE `Which item 23 column am I in` IS
    BRANCH IF age LESS THAN 35 THEN `Item 23 column` OF 0.04,   480,  0.16,   0.08,  7680
           IF age LESS THAN 45 THEN `Item 23 column` OF 0.045,  540,  0.18,   0.09,  8640
           IF age LESS THAN 50 THEN `Item 23 column` OF 0.05,   600,  0.2,    0.1,   9600
           OTHERWISE                `Item 23 column` OF 0.0525, 630,  0.21,   0.105, 10080
    WHERE
        age MEANS `How old am I taken to be for the year` `my year`

GIVEN `my year` IS A `My relevant year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the item 23 amount before rounding` IS
    BRANCH IF i AT MOST 6000  THEN 0
           IF i AT MOST 12000 THEN i TIMES c's `lower rate`
           IF i AT MOST 18000 THEN c's `middle base` PLUS c's `middle factor` TIMES (i MINUS 12000)
           IF i TIMES c's `top rate` GREATER THAN c's `top maximum` THEN c's `top maximum`
           OTHERWISE               i TIMES c's `top rate`
    WHERE
        i MEANS `What is my income under the Regulations` `my year`
        c MEANS `Which item 23 column am I in` `my year`

-- Reg 4(1)(m): I "must pay contributions into the Fund on his or her own behalf ... at the applicable rate specified in the second,
-- third, fourth and fifth columns of item 23 in the First Schedule".
-- Reg 14: "any fraction of a dollar is to be disregarded."
-- Reg 8A(1): the amount (C) "is to be reduced by the total amount of estimated contributions payable to the Fund under section 9B
-- ... (E) (if any)"; (2): "If E is more than C, the contribution payable ... is nil."
-- NOTHING where item 23 does not reach the case: a year before 2026, or a Member of Parliament.
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My relevant year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute for the year` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `my year`'s `the relevant year` LESS THAN 2026 THEN NOTHING
        IF `my year`'s `I am a Member of Parliament` THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `Do the Self-Employed Persons Regulations apply to me` `my year` THEN JUST 0
        IF e AT LEAST c THEN JUST 0
        OTHERWISE JUST (FLOOR (c MINUS e))
    WHERE
        c MEANS FLOOR (`the item 23 amount before rounding` `my year`)
        e MEANS `my year`'s `estimated contributions paid for me under section 9B`

§§ `Reg 7A(2) and (3) -- by when`

-- s 9A(1)(b): "before the expiry of the prescribed period, or any longer period that the Board specifies in any particular case".
-- Reg 7A(2): "A self-employed person must pay the contributions for each relevant year not later than -- (a) 30 days after the date
-- of issue of the notice of computation or contributions notice (as the case may be) for the relevant year; or (b) where the Board
-- specifies an extended period of payment ... the end of that extended period."
-- Reg 7A(3): the contributions "may be paid in instalments, so long as the total amount of those contributions is paid not later
-- than the time of payment applicable".
-- The notice's date of issue is the Board's act, so days are counted from it. INFERENCE (labelled): an "extended" period ends more
-- than 30 days after issue; 0 means the Board specified none.
GIVEN `the Board's extended period, in days after the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after the notice do I have to pay` IS
    IF   `the Board's extended period, in days after the notice` GREATER THAN 30
    THEN `the Board's extended period, in days after the notice`
    ELSE 30

GIVEN `what I owe` IS A NUMBER
      `what I have paid in total, in one sum or in instalments` IS A NUMBER
      `the day after the notice on which I made my last payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the Board's extended period, in days after the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I paid in time` IF
        `what I have paid in total, in one sum or in instalments` AT LEAST `what I owe`
    AND `the day after the notice on which I made my last payment`
            AT MOST `How many days after the notice do I have to pay` `the Board's extended period, in days after the notice`

§§ `9(2), 9(3), 58(1)(e) and 61(1) -- if I do not pay`

-- s 9(2): where the contributions are "not paid within the time prescribed for payment, that person is liable to pay interest on
-- that amount for every day the amount remains unpaid at the rate and commencing from the date prescribed in regulations".
-- s 9(3): "The Board may, in any case in which it thinks fit, waive the payment of the whole or part of, or remit ... any interest".
-- The rate is in no deposited instrument, so the encoding answers whether interest runs, not how much.
GIVEN `I paid in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board has waived the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay interest on my contributions` IF
    NOT `I paid in time` AND NOT `the Board has waived the interest`

-- s 58(1): "If any person -- ... (e) fails to pay to the Board within such period as may be prescribed any amount which the person
-- is liable to pay under the provisions of this Act, the person shall be guilty of an offence."
-- s 61(1): "any person convicted of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided shall be liable on conviction --
-- (a) to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both; and (b) if that person is a
-- repeat offender in relation to the same offence, to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 12 months or to both." s 61(2)'s minimum fines attach only to ss 7(5), 8A(5) and 58(1)(b), so there is no minimum here.
-- s 61(3): a repeat offender has "been convicted of the same offence on at least one other occasion".
GIVEN `I have been convicted of not paying on at least one other occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not paying my contributions` IS
    IF `I have been convicted of not paying on at least one other occasion` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `I have been convicted of not paying on at least one other occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for not paying, in months` IS
    IF `I have been convicted of not paying on at least one other occasion` THEN 12 ELSE 6
